  "representation_differences": [
    "C sign-extension arithmetic is expressed with fixed-width bitcasts/subtraction in Zig; every resulting i64 bit pattern is identical.",
    "Mixed-endian float support is absent from the pinned ABI/profile; big-endian record bits are bitcast to the host IEEE-754 f64 exactly as the active C branch.",
    "The constant 128-byte size table is compile-time generated from the same fixed exceptional entries and alternating payload formula."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "protocol": "The shared worker decodes serial types 0 through 15 plus 127, 128, 129, 255, and 256 from sign-sensitive bytes, compares both length APIs, flags, n, union bits, and ephemeral pointer identity, then directly exercises serialGet7 with finite 1.0 and a NaN payload. C and Zig compare 363 observations.",
    "internal_observations": [
